I planned to make a more self improvement centered journal next.. but this is what is mainly on my mind right now and I've always been curious if other people experience this too. <br>
Hmm, how do I explain it, sometimes, going throughout my day, and this usually fluctuates depending on my mood, what I'm doing, what has been happening recently, what I have lined up for the future etc. <br>
I usually have what i like to call "hits of conciousness".<br>
It usually occurs when I'm lost in a task, for example coding, writing, playing music, watching a show or movie, or especially listening to music. It's like, one moment I am really enjoying what's happening right now, and then for just a split second, it's like I "lose myself". The next moment I'm sort of looking around, firstly taking note of my environment, what's happening right now, how I feel, etc. I react that way because in moments where I feel a little lost, my mind jumps to kind of instinctively "grounding" myself, by sort of noticing my tether to reality and what's just kind of happening, who I am, etc. A lot of self talk is important to me.<br> 
But yeah, after this kind of thing happens, I start thinking about, well, how that just happened. Like, "Hey, I just had one of those moments again!" And then, thinking that thought, usually leads to me turning on my meta-cognition side of thinking. Meta-cognition is very simply thinking about thoughts. And I say my meta-cognition side of thinking, because It feels like my brain turns on a sort of different "mode" of thinking. <br>
Do you get what I'm saying? Like there's different "modes" my brain can be in. Like, Im in gym mode, where im just kind of focused on the next workout, or Im in music mode where Im just flowing and thinking of what's next in the song, or I'm in social mode and im thinking of what to say next, how I'm making the other person feel, how they feel, what they would probably want to talk about, what I can learn from them, etc. <br>
Anyway, I also have this kind of "mode" where I reflect on my thoughts. Sometimes I even reflect on my reflections to see if im reflecting how I want to. Whew, this kind of feels like a lot of layers now that I'm typing it out. It feels a lot simpler in my brain. <br>
I do really like being in this mode though. It makes me feel like I'm really *experiencing* something, if that makes any sense. It usually leads to a lot of gratitude. And by extension, because I like being in this metacognition mode, I really like getting hits of conciousness. <br>
Some of the most memorable hits happen when I'm like, around friends. Like im flowing socially, I'm feeling really happy and extroverted being around people and laughing and stuff, and then the next moment I'm looking around and thinking "Wow, i'm experiencing this situation right now. Im with #### and #### right now. This is great." and I get really happy. And then I think "Hmm I wonder if Im a weirdo for thinking this way. Maybe I should write a journal about that." I don't know. something like that. <br>
anyway ya let me know if you guys relate to this at all lolol love u all